/-
# Tests.AnchorsShufM — D362: the shuffle path's memory shapes, `pextrd`/`pextrq` to memory and `pinsrq` from m64

The 56 rows `hwprobe/shuf_probe.c` runs for the three shapes D336 did not take, pinned to this model in their OWN metered
unit (arm (A) of the 2026-10-10 kernel-cost fork, as every silicon batch since): `Tests.AnchorsShuf`'s Δku allowance
(23.3 % of 511,292) is smaller than these rows at its per-row rate. Each pin compares all of XMM0, all of RAX, the six
arithmetic flags AND the 16 bytes at 0x2000 ([RBX]), exactly as the probe does, so a store is compared beyond its own
width and a dropped store reds.

The block between the markers is GENERATED by `hwprobe/mk_shuf_anchors.py --d362` (`--check` gates it byte for byte).

LANE. Personal lane, public sources only.
-/
import X86

namespace X86.Tests.ShufM
open X86

/-! ## D362 — pinned to hwprobe's rows

x86isa refuses all three encodings at 88 of 88 pre-states (D362's P1), so these rows are the only check of the model's
numbers for them. The three helpers are `Tests.AnchorsShuf`'s, restated because those are private to their module. -/

private def v1bFlags (f : BitVec 64) : Flags :=
  ⟨f.getLsbD 0, f.getLsbD 2, f.getLsbD 4, f.getLsbD 6, f.getLsbD 7, f.getLsbD 11, false⟩

private def v1bRflags (f : Flags) : BitVec 64 :=
  flagFields.foldl (fun acc r => acc ||| (if r.get f then (1 : BitVec 64) <<< r.bit else 0)) 0

/-- `shuf_ops.S`'s pre-state, at RIP 0x400000: XMM0 = a, XMM1 = b, b's 16 bytes at 0x2000 = RBX, RCX = g, RAX the
canary. -/
private def v1bPre (a b : BitVec 128) (g f : BitVec 64) : Cpu :=
  let r : Regs := ((({} : Regs).set .rax 0xc3c3c3c3c3c3c3c3).set .rcx g).set .rbx 0x2000
  ((({ regs := r, flags := v1bFlags f, mem := {}, rip := 0x400000, oracle := Oracle.zero } : Cpu).setXmm .x0 a).setXmm
    .x1 b).writeMem128 0x2000 b

/-- `Tests.AnchorsShuf`'s `v1bAgrees`, plus the 16 bytes at 0x2000 after the instruction. -/
private def v362Agrees (t : Cpu) (n : Nat) (f : BitVec 64) (wr : BitVec 128) (wax : BitVec 64) (wm : BitVec 128) :
    Bool :=
  t.ms.isNone && t.getXmm .x0 == wr && t.regs.get .rax == wax
    && (v1bRflags t.flags &&& 0x8d5) == (f &&& 0x8d5) && t.rip == 0x400000 + BitVec.ofNat 64 n
    && t.readMem128 0x2000 == wm

